sary, broad, or destructive mutations were found; failed-services and package-health checks show no damage after_executor.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-915e57bdec0a4f6f\",\"cmd-eafe6b9a7aa640d0\",\"cmd-075f23924c594c98\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task — blocking usb-storage from loading immediately and persisting the block across reboot — are satisfied with direct, coherent evidence. The executor wrote a modprobe.d blacklist/install-false config, verified an immediate modprobe failure, regenerated and confirmed a clean initramfs, then executed a real reboot (verified via boot_id change from a70d7f83... to a8628c34...) and re-verified post-reboot that the module remains blocked. This fulfills the stricter evidentiary bar required for persistence/reboot claims (healthy baseline, disruption, restoration, recovered state all directly observed).\",\"limitations\":[\"Lifecycle before_prepare/after_prepare snapshots are identical (prepare disabled), limiting their usefulness for isolating preparer- vs executor-caused state, though this does not affect assessment of executor actions since all state changes were captured in the executor timeline.\",\"The /tmp/reboot.log artifact left behind is minor residue from the reboot mechanism and was not explicitly cleaned up, though it has no functional impact.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"block-now","requirement":"Stop usb-storage module from loading immediately","status":"satisfied","summary":"Baseline confirmed module not loaded; /etc/modprobe.d/blacklist-usb-storage.conf written with blacklist + install /bin/false directives; modprobe usb-storage immediately failed with 'could not insert usb_storage: Invalid argument', directly demonstrating the block is active now.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7f06b270ebd146a6","cmd-915e57bdec0a4f6f","cmd-eafe6b9a7aa640d0"]},{"id":"block-persistent","requirement":"